SUMMARY:Detecting Non-Linear Gravitational Wave Memory and Beyond
DESCRIPTION:Séminaire Amplitudes et Gravitation sur l'Yvette (IHES/IPhT) G
 ravitational-wave (GW) memory is a non-oscillatory component of GW signals
  that leaves a permanent displacement in spacetime after the wave has pass
 ed. It is a generic prediction of General Relativity\, arising at second o
 rder from the nonlinear dynamics of gravity\, yet it has not been detected
  so far. In this talk\, I will present…\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/eve
 nt/17927/
